meta {
  name: payment testing
}

docs {
  # Payment testing collection

  Three self-contained scenarios for the tab / Stripe authorize-then-capture
  flow. Each subfolder creates its own attendee session + tab, so any folder can
  be run on its own. Run with the Bruno runner; requests within a folder reuse
  runtime vars (`bru.setVar`) set by earlier ones.

  IMPORTANT: select the **Dev** environment first, otherwise `{{host}}` /
  `{{port}}` are empty and URLs are invalid.

  ## Why the Stripe "confirm" steps exist
  Checkout calls the real `stripe.paymentIntents.capture()`. Simulating our own
  webhook only flips the TabPayment to AUTHORIZED in our DB; on Stripe's side the
  PaymentIntent is still unconfirmed and not capturable, so checkout would 500.
  Each hold that gets captured is therefore first confirmed against the real
  Stripe test API with `pm_card_visa`. The webhook simulation is still needed to
  update our DB, since Stripe cannot reach localhost without the Stripe CLI.

  Prerequisites:
  - Dev env: `eventId` is an ACTIVE event with `standId` / `productId` under it;
    product price well below the EUR 10.00 (1000 cents) baseline hold.
  - `stripeSecretKey` (Dev env) is the project's Stripe TEST secret key.
  - Backend runs in dev so /webhooks/stripe accepts unsigned JSON.

  ## Folders
  1. order under baseline   — one item within the hold; checkout captures only
     the consumed amount.
  2. over threshold succeeds — under-order, then an order over the hold whose
     overage hold is authorized; checkout captures baseline + overage.
  3. payment fails           — order over the hold whose overage payment fails;
     tab reopens; checkout captures the baseline only (1000).
}
